        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="span">Based on the principles of HCI, a good web design should present a user-friendly web interface to access the information they need.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">A user-friendly web interface should make web users feel easy to access the information that web users need.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="12" relname="span">Also, usability is another important criteria to measure</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="condition">if a web page/site is a good web page/site.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="13" relname="span">A good web page/site should deliver the best and the most current information for web users.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="antithesis">Without this premiss, no texts, fonts, colors, images, audio/video components, programming, web servers, and databases can play their roles in a good web design.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="9" relname="summary">To sum up, Usability, Accessibility, User-friendly, Quality, and Performance should become the essential criteria to measure a good web design.</segment>
        <group id="8" type="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="8" relname="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="10" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
</rst>
